msgid "Abstract base class for hash table data structures."
msgstr ""

#: 8121596b3cc841b6bcf4856f8aee5e64 of
#: sds.advanced.interfaces.AbstractHashTable:3
msgid ""
"A hash table maps keys to values using a hash function to compute an "
"index into an array of buckets or slots. Concrete subclasses implement "
"different collision-resolution strategies."
msgstr ""

#: c7dad8c780b54cba8a132df3b03ef064 of
#: sds.advanced.interfaces.AbstractHashTable:9
msgid "Two classical collision-resolution strategies are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: 26ea7cd7fc5c4866872c9086916e8330 of
#: sds.advanced.interfaces.AbstractHashTable:11
msgid ""
"**Separate chaining**: each slot holds a list of (key, value) pairs. "
"Worst-case O(n) per operation, O(1) average with a good hash function and"
" load factor ≤ 1."
msgstr ""

#: 6682d78646d84690965736a6dec79b9c of
#: sds.advanced.interfaces.AbstractHashTable:14
msgid ""
"**Open addressing** (linear probing): all entries live in the array; "
"collisions are resolved by probing subsequent slots. Worst-case O(n), "
"O(1) average for load factor < 0.7."
msgstr ""

#: 4fd720b9405543cb93eba306e2aea3a2 of
#: sds.advanced.interfaces.AbstractHashTable:18
msgid ""
"Both implementations resize automatically when the load factor exceeds a "
"configurable threshold."
msgstr ""

#: 8962b41a66834a0bad376cd9109d8903 of
#: sds.advanced.interfaces.AbstractHashTable:23
msgid ":obj:`HashTableChaining`"
msgstr ""

#: 341a8f7d2e7a4e3cb870d3263152c330 of
#: sds.advanced.interfaces.AbstractHashTable:24
msgid "Separate-chaining implementation."
msgstr ""

#: 2b2a6e8b138e434db664c5e5002e9182 of
